WEBVTT

00:00:10.975 --> 00:00:11.839
Hi there.

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:14.719
Welcome to this video
where we are going to learn about

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:17.791
what it means to be resilient
in digital environments.

00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:22.831
The goal of the video is to help you
to understand what resilience is,

00:00:22.911 --> 00:00:24.191
and things that you can do

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:27.759
to help yourself to become 
more resilient in digital environments.

00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:32.511
In the video, firstly, we will
look at what we mean by resilience.

00:00:33.119 --> 00:00:36.031
Then we will look at things
we can do to help us

00:00:36.031 --> 00:00:39.039
to become more resilient.

00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:46.559
According to the dictionary, 
resilience is the ability to cope

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:50.351
when exposed to challenges
or things that cause you to feel stressed.

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:55.439
Resilience allows people to bounce back
by adapting to stress in healthy way.

00:00:56.271 --> 00:00:59.439
The digital world
can sometimes expose us to a number

00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:03.679
of challenges, such as negative
or hateful comments, identity

00:01:03.711 --> 00:01:07.391
theft and fraud, and exclusion
by others on social media.

00:01:08.111 --> 00:01:13.631
This can leave us feeling sad, anxious,
angry, or a lot of different emotions.

00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:17.791
We may also feel a bit powerless
and not know what to do.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:23.199
Sometimes we may be able to handle
the challenges we face by being resilient.

00:01:24.047 --> 00:01:26.495
Resilience is a skill, and we can learn

00:01:26.495 --> 00:01:29.855
how to be resilient and bounce 
forward from these challenges.

00:01:29.935 --> 00:01:30.735
Get up.

00:01:30.735 --> 00:01:33.855
Learn from what you have 
experienced and move forwards.

00:01:39.135 --> 00:01:40.063
Step one:

00:01:40.063 --> 00:01:43.215
Acknowledging the challenge
and or stressor and use

00:01:43.215 --> 00:01:46.223
problem solving techniques 
to resolve the issue.

00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:49.615
It shows wisdom to acknowledge
that there is a challenge.

00:01:49.855 --> 00:01:52.863
This is a good starting point
to solving the challenge.

00:01:53.663 --> 00:01:58.095
Step two: Seeking support to gain
an alternative viewpoint on the issue.

00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:01.775
You can sometimes solve 
challenges on your own.

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:06.143
Other times, it can be wise to accept
that you need help and to ask for help.

00:02:06.815 --> 00:02:10.623
We can chat to someone we trust
like a parent or a teacher for help.

00:02:10.735 --> 00:02:13.743
Or call a trusted 
kid's helpline for a chat.

00:02:13.855 --> 00:02:17.295
Step three: Implementing
self-care strategies.

00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:22.495
Sometimes you can find small things
that help you to calm your thoughts and feelings.

00:02:22.495 --> 00:02:25.935
This can help you think 
more clearly and be more resilient.

00:02:26.655 --> 00:02:28.975
These are called coping strategies

00:02:28.975 --> 00:02:31.935
or self-care strategies.

00:02:31.935 --> 00:02:34.815
It is wise to know what is helpful to you.

00:02:34.815 --> 00:02:37.823
What little things help you feel calmer?

00:02:37.855 --> 00:02:40.942
Some examples of things 
that people do to help them to cope

00:02:40.942 --> 00:02:44.414
and care for themselves
when facing challenges are activities

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:49.262
with others such as playing
sport, dancing, helping someone, singing.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:53.534
Some activities can also 
be done alone, such as drawing,

00:02:53.662 --> 00:02:58.462
slow breathing, spending time with a pet,
listening to music, reading a book,

00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:01.182
writing a journal, gaming.

00:03:01.182 --> 00:03:04.654
Step four: Gain sufficient 
distance from the problem

00:03:04.702 --> 00:03:06.542
to alleviate some of the pressure.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:11.294
Sometimes it can be wise to take 
a break and do something that you enjoy.

00:03:12.094 --> 00:03:15.534
This can help you to get some distance
from the challenge you are facing.

00:03:16.254 --> 00:03:19.934
It can give you a new perspective
and help you to feel better.

00:03:20.814 --> 00:03:25.614
Step five recognize that everyone
makes mistakes in the digital environment.

00:03:26.094 --> 00:03:28.974
So next time you feel sad
because somebody says something

00:03:28.974 --> 00:03:32.462
mean to you in a group chat,
or when you share something by mistake.

00:03:32.622 --> 00:03:37.134
Remember these coping strategies
reflect over the challenging situation.

00:03:37.838 --> 00:03:40.830
Is there something that you can learn
from the situation?

00:03:41.374 --> 00:03:44.606
Is there something positive
that you can take from the experience

00:03:44.606 --> 00:03:47.614
that may help you
or someone else in the future?

00:03:48.302 --> 00:03:51.694
So in this short video,
we learned what we mean by resilience

00:03:51.774 --> 00:03:55.262
and looked at things we can do 
to help us to become more resilient.

00:03:58.782 --> 00:04:00.350
Thank you for watching.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:03.310
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.

